  "query_preview": "..FOR EXTREME SOUTHWESTERN CALIFORNIA INCLUDING ORANGE...\nSAN DIEGO...WESTERN RIVERSIDE AND SOUTHWESTERN SAN BERNARDINO\nCOUNTIES...\n\n...Updated Aviation and Marine discussions...\n\nThis afternoon...The marine layer remains about 1500 feet deep with \na strong inversion so low clouds are persisting at the immediate \ncoast. Low clouds will likely begin to spread inland in the late \nafternoon. Temperatures are mostly within a few degrees of what they \nwere 24 hours ago. A closed upper low to the southwest is enabling \nsome high clouds to move into SoCal from the south in the southerly \nflow aloft.\n\nHigh temperatures today will range from the lower to mid 70s near\nthe coast to the mid 80s to mid 90s in the Inland Empire with 106\nto 110 for the lower deserts. High temperatures inland will rise \nslightly for tomorrow and Saturday. In the coastal areas, temperatures\nwill be within a few degrees each day. Through Saturday, high \ntemperatures will generally range from a few degrees above average\nnear the coast to 5 to 10 degrees above average for the mountains\nand deserts. Moderate HeatRisk will continue for the deserts into\nnext week with the greatest coverage of moderate HeatRisk for the\nInland Empire on Friday.\n\nThe weak upper low centered about 200 miles off the coast of\ncentral Baja will continue to push moisture from northern Baja\ninto SoCal over the next 24-48 hours as it drifts slowly westward.\nEnough mid-level moisture could spread into the region on Friday \nfor there to be small chances for showers over the mountains in\nthe afternoon. The increasing moisture aloft will likely inhibit\nthe radiation cooling overnight so that low temperatures will\nremain above seasonal averages, and some locations could\nexperience record high minimum temperatures.\n\nHigh temperatures for the mountains and deserts will remain around\n4 to 8 degrees above average through next Wednesday. For the \ncoast and valleys, high temperatures will cool a few degrees from\nSunday through Wednesday, cooling from within a few degrees of \naverage on Sunday to a few degrees below average on Wednesday. \nHigh temperatures on Sunday will range from the lower to mid 70s \nnear the coast to the mid 80s to mid 90s for the Inland Empire \nwith 108 to 112 for the lower deserts. Moderate HeatRisk will \ncontinue for the deserts through next Wednesday. Night and morning\ncoastal low clouds will spread inland into the western valleys at\ntimes.",
